@Declarations
.
=DECLARATIONS
.
.DIM and VAR mean the same thing. Every variable must be declared.
.
=DIM ... AT
.
.DIM name AS type AT address puts a number variable at a fixed address. The
.variable takes no space in the program.
.
:DIM REG_A AS UBYTE AT $030C, REG_P AS UBYTE AT $030F
:REG_P = 0
:REG_A = 65
:SYS $FFD2                    ' CHROUT prints A
:IF REG_P AND 1 THEN PRINT "CARRY"
.
.  - The address is a constant expression: DIM H AS UBYTE AT $0400 + 1.
.  - A WORD or UWORD takes the address and the next byte, low byte first. A
.    LONG or ULONG takes 4 bytes.
.  - The variable works wherever a variable does: in expressions, as the
.    target of =, as a FOR counter, in INPUT and as a BIND target.
.  - Each read or write is one absolute load or store, 3 bytes, also at a
.    zero-page address. REG_P = 5 is LDA #5, STA $030F.
.  - AddrOf(name) is the address. In ASM it is two bytes.
.  - Two variables may share an address: DIM P AS UWORD AT $0400, L AS UBYTE
.    AT $0400.
.  - The address is not checked against the program's own memory.
.  - An address that is not a constant stops the compile with ADDRESS NOT A
.    CONSTANT.
.  - An array or a string with AT stops the compile with NOT YET: AN ARRAY OR
.    A STRING AT AN ADDRESS.
.
.See Types, SYS, Pointers.
.
